{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/troubleshooting"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Troubleshooting"},"abstract":[{"text":"Symptoms you may hit while adopting Swidux, and what each one actually means.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Xcode-asks-to-Trust--Enable-a-macro","level":2,"text":"Xcode asks to “Trust & Enable” a macro"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are compiler plugins, so the first build in Xcode"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"prompts once per machine to trust the "},{"code":"SwiduxMacros","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" target. Approve it in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"build error’s fix-it or under "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Settings → Packages","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":". On CI, pass"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"-skipMacroValidation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"code":"xcodebuild","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead — there’s no one to click the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dialog.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"The first build is slow","level":2,"anchor":"The-first-build-is-slow"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux depends on "},{"code":"swift-syntax","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which the macro system compiles from source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on first build (a few minutes on CI-class hardware). It’s cached afterwards;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing is wrong. CI pipelines benefit from caching "},{"code":".build\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or DerivedData."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Console shows “Re-entrant Store.send(…) — deferring”","level":2,"anchor":"Console-shows-Re-entrant-Storesend-deferring"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Something called "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.send"},{"type":"text","text":" synchronously from inside a reducer or plugin"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hook — usually a plugin observing state and dispatching in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", or a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Binding"},{"type":"text","text":" setter fired during view updates. The store defers the inner action"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and runs it as a full cycle right after the current one, so state stays"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consistent — but the fault log is telling you the design wants that follow-up"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dispatched from an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Effect"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"`call to main actor-isolated initializer … in a synchronous nonisolated context`","level":2,"anchor":"call-to-main-actor-isolated-initializer--in-a-synchronous-nonisolated-context"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The module is compiling in Swift 5 language mode with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SWIFT_DEFAULT_ACTOR_ISOLATION = MainActor"},{"text":". A ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Swidux nonisolated struct","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only gets a nonisolated synthesized memberwise initializer under ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift 6"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mode"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"SWIFT_VERSION = 6.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"); under Swift 5 mode the macro’s state","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reconstruction can’t call it, and adding an explicit ","type":"text"},{"code":"nonisolated init","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not rescue it. Switch the target to Swift 6 mode.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Error-stored-properties-need-an-explicit-type-annotation","type":"heading","text":"Error: “stored properties need an explicit type annotation”"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"var flag = false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives the compiler an inferred type, but macros can’t see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it — before this diagnostic existed, such a property was silently skipped and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its value reset on every dispatch. Write ","type":"text"},{"code":"var flag: Bool = false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"applies to combined declarations: split ","type":"text"},{"code":"var a, b: Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" into separate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declarations.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Keychain-writes-fail-with-OSStatus-%E2%88%9234018-errSecMissingEntitlement","type":"heading","text":"Keychain writes fail with OSStatus −34018 (`errSecMissingEntitlement`)"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An unsigned local or CI build is using ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore"},{"text":" without a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"provisioning profile. This is a signing condition, not a prompt or a bug — the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"data-protection keychain never prompts.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing is persisted, but nothing crashes either: the write logs, returns"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":", and the app continues. Ship provisioning-profile-signed builds with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accessGroup: nil"},{"type":"text","text":" to get real persistence."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Adding a team-prefixed "},{"code":"keychain-access-groups","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" entitlement also works, and is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the right call when you want the access group — but weigh it first, because it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"makes the app require a provisioning profile for every signed build. It is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" a fix for a test host: "},{"code":"CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" embeds no entitlements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at all, so there is nothing for the entitlement to attach to. Let the write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degrade there. Details in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"`Test crashed with signal trap before establishing connection`","anchor":"Test-crashed-with-signal-trap-before-establishing-connection","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"xcodebuild test","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" dies before any test runs, naming nothing useful. If the app","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mints a device identity or writes a token at launch, suspect the Keychain: the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"test host is unsigned, the write fails, and a trap takes the process down before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the test bundle can attach.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Current versions degrade instead of trapping here, so upgrading Swidux is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fix. To confirm the diagnosis on an older one, run the same scheme with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=YES"},{"type":"text","text":" — if it gets past launch, the Keychain was the cause."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Edits-disappear-after-a-sync-tick-or-an-async-load","text":"Edits disappear after a sync tick or an async load","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Symptom: a keystroke, a toggle, or a whole entity vanishes — intermittently,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"usually while something is loading or syncing, and never reproducibly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The cause is almost always a hand-rolled bridge from ","type":"text"},{"code":"async","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" work into the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store. ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keeps state in an ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" observer tree and converts to a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value-type snapshot on the way in and out (“pack” and “unpack”). If you pack a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"snapshot, ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" something, and then unpack it, everything dispatched during","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is silently overwritten:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var snapshot = AppState(observer: store.observer)   \/\/ ← packed BEFORE the await","await loadEverything(into: &snapshot)               \/\/ ← dispatches land here…","AppState.apply(snapshot, to: store.observer)        \/\/ ← …and are discarded here"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" across a suspension point is the tell. The window is only as wide"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as the "},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which is why it presents as a rare glitch rather than a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reproducible bug."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/mutate(awaiting:merging:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" instead. It runs the async work with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"access to state, then packs a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"fresh","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" snapshot, merges, and unpacks in a single","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"step with no suspension point in between — so no dispatch can interleave:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["await store.mutate {","    try await api.fetchItems()          \/\/ no state in scope; nothing to stale","} merging: { items, state in","    state.items.merge(from: EntityStore(items)) { _, _ in false }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The persistence stack’s own async entry points already work this way — use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"persistence.rehydrate(into: store)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sync.setSyncEnabled(_:into: store)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not a snapshot you manage yourself. (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hydrate(into: &state)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the exception,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and safe: it runs at launch, before the store exists.)"}]},{"anchor":"Contributors-the-lint-plugin-doesnt-run--dev-tooling-is-missing","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Contributors: the lint plugin doesn’t run \/ dev tooling is missing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Dev tooling (the Persnoop linter, the DocC plugin) is gated behind a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gitignored "},{"code":".dev-tooling","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sentinel file so it never leaks into consumers’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dependency graphs. Create it at the package root — and if the package was"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already built without it, run "},{"code":"swift package purge-cache","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" so SwiftPM re-reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the manifest. See the repository’s "},{"code":"CONTRIBUTING.md","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"A-Persisted-app-crashes-only-in-Release","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"A `@Persisted` app crashes only in Release"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If the crash is in fetching, make sure you’re on ≥ 1.3.0: generic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#Predicate"},{"text":" over a protocol-required keypath traps under ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-O"},{"text":", which is why","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the macro generates a per-model ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swiduxBatchFetchDescriptor"},{"text":" — one for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one for ","type":"text"},{"code":"persistentModelID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — and why every by-identifier read goes through","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one instead of building a predicate inline. Run ","type":"text"},{"code":"swift test -c release","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in CI","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to catch this class of issue — Debug builds and default ","type":"text"},{"code":"swift test","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pass.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Reference","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityEditingGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistedAssociations","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"],"title":"Reference"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"title":"Swidux","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginAnalyticsReference":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" library — provider-agnostic analytics with declarative event mapping, auto-identify, and explicit dispatch for the cases the mapper can’t cover."}],"title":"SwiduxAnalytics Reference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginanalyticsreference","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/mutate(awaiting:merging:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/mutate(awaiting:merging:)","kind":"symbol","title":"mutate(awaiting:merging:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"mutate","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Value"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"awaiting","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": () "},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"text":"merging","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"State","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Void","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"rethrows"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Runs async work that must not hold state across its suspensions, then","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"folds the result into a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"freshly packed","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" snapshot in one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"suspension-free step.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/mutate(awaiting:merging:)"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"UndoPlugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStoreGuide":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection with built-in change tracking."}],"title":"EntityStore","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystoreguide","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginParentalGateReference":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API surface for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"type":"text","text":" library — a domain plugin that guards actions behind a math challenge."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginparentalgatereference","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"SwiduxParentalGate Reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistedAssociations":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistedAssociations","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Persisting canonical associations","abstract":[{"text":"Declare parent and child identities separately, then save an editing session through one local transaction.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistedassociations","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted","type":"topic","role":"article",